{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts","id":1495178,"title":"M20 Sorcerer dropped, What are everyone's thoughts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-18T12:38:55-07:00","id":1495178,"title":"M20 Sorcerer dropped, What are everyone's thoughts?","content":"M20 Sorcerer dropped last Wednesday and everyone who ordered an advanced copy had theirs updated to the final product the day before then.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm mixed.<br /> <br /> They kept in the more fundamental issues that were in the advanced release and other versions prior. The weird aspect/difficulty interaction is still there in full force(and the &quot;optional \u0336f\u0336i\u0336x\u0336 /rule&quot; misses the point <i>Hard</i>), some paths ignore the aspect system entirely even when it doesn't completely make sense(alchemy using duration would have been fine) and the turn-per dot casting that Everyone pointed out was a bad idea was left as-is(hand guns take only a turn to shoot, do more damage, and draw less attention than a fireball in comparison).<br /> <br /> A new issue has cropped up in that Sorcerers have no inherent means of gaining and storing mana/quintessence. The mana background was scrapped entirely and Avatar was one of few mage backgrounds that was Not made available for sorcerers to take. This renders the Merits Flow of Ki, Strength of Psyche, and Force of Spirit are now practically useless in most situations. It's currently impossible for sorcerers to use Quint without a specific path <i>At the 4th dot or Higher</i>(on a side note, the &quot;draw quintessence for node&quot; ability was placed at 4 dots, and the &quot;store quintessence in object&quot; was placed at 3 dots(2 with a ritual). This means you can't get the quintessence to store in an object until path level4). Sorcerers even at their maximum cannot hold quint for more than a turn, so they must spend a prior action gaining quintessence somehow before they can use quint for a merit or spell(effectively doubling quintessence's turn requirements in the action economy).<br /> <br /> On the other hand I like how much many of the systems have been cleaned up and organized. I really like how they handled the psychic powers system especially and how plug-and-play it makes creating a psychic character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T15:30:17-07:00","id":1495196,"title":"","content":"Yeah; that bit about Quintessence is getting changed in my games, through the simple expedient of acknowledging that even Sleepers have Avatars; they're just, well, Sleeping. You get the mechanical benefits of the Background, but not the \u201cvoice in your head\u201d goading you on.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I still prefer <b>Sorcerer: Paths of Power</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-18-2022, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T15:54:40-07:00","id":1495198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495196#post1495196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; that bit about Quintessence is getting changed in my games, through the simple expedient of acknowledging that even Sleepers have Avatars; they're just, well, Sleeping. You get the mechanical benefits of the Background, but not the \u201cvoice in your head\u201d goading you on.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are you handling the XP costs?<br /> <br /> Personally going to tone them down Hard. Current costs are at out-of-clan discipline/near mage-sphere levels despite being orders of magnitude weaker. Despite path power being comparable, a Vamp thaumaturge only pays dot x4 XP for paths after the first.<br /> <br /> Why are Numina so expensive in comparison?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T16:06:31-07:00","id":1495199,"title":"","content":"My POD copy is coming (there was no way I wasn't buying it in print) but yeah I too am not entirely sure about some of the changes/features, etc. <br /> <br /> I do know that there will be elements I change hard in it - Aspects are the 'you get them equal to path rating for a single success' is my standard, and Passengers o not bringing clothes is something I find that ridiculous. The time on Hellifre being multiple turns is also meh. The whole Quintessence Manipulation path. <br /> <br /> But yeah I do thin some parts are better than it was. <br /> <br /> Oh, I am considering using the rule in Revised that changes difficulty to 3 + rating and also makes turns 2 dots per turn (so 1 and 2 dot powers take a turn). Bringing XP down to thaumaturgy levels makes a to of sense to me as well. <br /> <br /> So yeah I would totally be interested in reading more of your thoughts about this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T16:54:18-07:00","id":1495204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495199#post1495199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do know that there will be elements I change hard in it - Aspects are the 'you get them equal to path rating for a single success' is my standard, and Passengers o not bringing clothes is something I find that ridiculous. The time on Hellifre being multiple turns is also meh. The whole Quintessence Manipulation path.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal take for aspects is at least 1 success in the spell roll = All aspects start at 1 automatically without allocation, additional successes are added on.<br /> <br /> I also pick a &quot;Specialty&quot; aspect for each path. That specialty is always has successes allocated equal to the dot rating of the path used, with an added downside that this aspect Cannot go over the dot rating, but non-specialty aspects can have more successes allocate than the dot rating.<br /> <br /> A hellfire user for example would be able to affect multiple people or snipe from far away with Hellfire 1, but their damage would be locked at Hellfire 1 levels. A spirit binder might always be able to call a powerful spirit at SBW 5, but the duration of the spell would be variable based on successes.<br /> <br /> This way difficulty is determined by the &quot;power&quot; of the spell being cast and successes are spent to see how well the sell went off. This avoid &quot;I used Path 1 with 10 dice and nothing to spend successes on while the player next to me used path 5 and didn't get enough successes to justify using the spell at that level&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495199#post1495199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah I do thin some parts are better than it was.<br /> <br /> Oh, I am considering using the rule in Revised that changes difficulty to 3 + rating and also makes turns 2 dots per turn (so 1 and 2 dot powers take a turn). Bringing XP down to thaumaturgy levels makes a to of sense to me as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re-reading the thaum rule reminded me how weird they are as well. A thaumaturge's primary path is their most expensive by far(being dot x7 unless tremere), but secondary path XP doesn't depend on clan so everyone gets dot x4 after that.(maybe because ritual knowledge is based on main path?)<br /> <br /> I'm thinking a fair amount for sorcerer might be dot x5, considering unlike blood magic every new path gives new rituals as well.<br /> <br /> As for the Good bits in the book, Psychics definitely got the lion's share of the the love. Several powers are much stronger than before in addition to basing all their rolls on willpower now. A notable one is Synergy(the hold hands and share powers ability), the power that let's psychics combine different powers into one Super ability was reduced from the 5th dot to 4th and the New 5th dot ability allows Psychics to use any Synergy with unlimited range. With that a group could send their beefiest guy to pentex headquarters and load him up with unlimited willpower and every psychic power Ever or summon Captain Planet at his location while porting him out of danger. Psychic cults are a genuine Main-splat-level threat now.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers have the comparable ability to cast grand rituals, which don't cost XP but does take several hours to do because of the sorcerer casting rule and can only be done with all the sorcerers in the same room actively helping. I think the writer had a bit of a bias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T06:42:21-07:00","id":1495238,"title":"","content":"While the aspect system in M20 is better than it was in Revised I still really don't care for it. I think it creates undo complication to the system and ultimately, I just find the systems from Sorcerer: Paths of Power to be more in line with what I want out of sorcery.<br /> <br /> Mana is a weird spot for me. I like the idea of Mana or at least a small pool for sorcerers to do spells/rituals/rotes/etc but, I don't think it's handled well here. I think at my table I'm going to let mortal sorcerers (as in 100% vanilla humans) have a mana pool of 2 just like how other half-splats have their power pools of 2, (Revenants have 2 blood they can spend, Kinian have 2 Glamour) I might bump this up to just say a flat rule of &quot;Half-Splats have their Stamina Scores in Resource.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T08:30:54-07:00","id":1495245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495238#post1495238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">half-splats have their power pools of 2(<b>Revenants have 2 blood they can spend</b>, Kinian have 2 Glamour) I might bump this up to just say a flat rule of &quot;Half-Splats have their Stamina Scores in Resource.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's a thing, standard ghouls have a blood pool of 2 before overfeeding, but revenants and dhampire have a pool of 10, kinfolk have a <i>Starting</i> gnosis pool of 1-3, spectre cultists had a being/passion stat of 1-10 based on contract(but they're now in a weird position with WtO20), etc. Even sorcerer's weren't limited to 5 man originally. One of the mana manipulation path abilities was to add your total dots in Mana manipulation to your mana background to determine your maximum pool. A starting sorcerer could end up with a pool of 10 if they invested heavily in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-20T20:57:51-07:00","id":1495343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts#post1495178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's currently impossible for sorcerers to use Quint without a specific path <i>At the 4th dot or Higher</i>(on a side note, the &quot;draw quintessence for node&quot; ability was placed at 4 dots, and the &quot;store quintessence in object&quot; was placed at 3 dots(2 with a ritual). This means you can't get the quintessence to store in an object until path level4).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerers without Quintessence Manipulation can use Tass. The shift in Quintessence use is intended to increase the importance of Tass for Sorcerers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T09:53:17-07:00","id":1495358,"title":"","content":"Overall, I think it's solid.<br /> <br /> The few quibbles I have with the crunch can be resolved with house rules, and presentation and fluff are really nice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T13:54:07-07:00","id":1495369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495343#post1495343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerers without Quintessence Manipulation can use Tass. The shift in Quintessence use is intended to increase the importance of Tass for Sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't tass supposed to be rare though? The only places it can reliably be found are inside powerful nodes and the bodies of supernatural creatures, either way good luck. Especially considering Sorcerers are limited by needing the correct resonance, which hurts more thanks to the fact that mastered quint manipulation no longer lets them alter resonance the way mana manipulation did.<br /> <br /> I think it achieves the opposite just because of how situational and limited quint is until higher levels combined with the amount of bookkeeping it'll take to keep track of all of the different sources and their resonances you'd need to make proper use of the path with current rules. I don't think quint see much use in many tables do to the availability of better alternatives in the available merit, ritual, and item creation rules(similar to what happened to earlier editions of resonance in most mage tables).<br /> <br /> I think having the avatar background like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> outlined and returning the resonance changing ability would offset this, but at that point we're honestly returning the old mana manipulation rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495358#post1495358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, I think it's solid.<br /> The few quibbles I have with the crunch can be resolved with house rules, and presentation and fluff are really nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely agree that the fluff is nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T14:23:18-07:00","id":1495371,"title":"","content":"Tass *is* supposed to be rare. How you get what you need, the rare components of a planned working, is one place where the story can be a great deal of fun for sorcerers.<br /> I encourage you to tweak the rules at your table to fit the feel you want, but each decision made from a development standpoint was to distinguish sorcerers from Mages and make them their own, unique thing. The magic is slow, and if you're working off the cuff or caught off guard or not prepared, you absolutely are better off with a pistol than a firebolt. However, sorcerers aren't &quot;off the cuff&quot; types. They've spent years studying arcane secrets to pry loose some scraps of wonder still remaining in the world and glean power from it. They are designed to be patient planners.<br /> <br /> Wiggling your nose and shooting a fireball is the realm of Magick, not sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":25411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","user":"TravisLegge","date":".  Edited for typos and capitalization issues 10-21-2022, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T15:02:02-07:00","id":1495375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495371#post1495371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tass *is* supposed to be rare. How you get what you need, the rare components of a planned working, is one place where the story can be a great deal of fun for sorcerers.<br /> I encourage you to tweak the rules at your table to fit the feel you want, but each decision made from a development standpoint was to distinguish sorcerers from Mages and make them their own, unique thing. The magic is slow, and if you're working off the cuff or caught off guard or not prepared, you absolutely are better off with a pistol than a firebolt. However, sorcerers aren't &quot;off the cuff&quot; types. They've spent years studying arcane secrets to pry loose some scraps of wonder still remaining in the world and glean power from it. They are designed to be patient planners.<br /> <br /> Wiggling your nose and shooting a fireball is the realm of Magick, not sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can understand your point, but I don't think this book accomplishes what you envision.<br /> <br /> Mages are able to do the slow methodical route as well, And do it vastly better than sorcerers. Enchanted objects, rituals and personal empowerments are all things mages do better in addition to fast-casting, which becomes even more of an issue with the fact that the XP costs for both are comparable. If sorcerers were given a way to equal what mages accomplish via the slow, methodical route or were given much more of and XP brake so that they could advance faster and/or branch out more, I'd agree.<br /> <br /> I think needing difficult and rare components for even the low levels of a path to work is too much personally, even without other factors. From a play standpoint, a player would either see very little use of the path or would need to invest heavily in it with the ST shaping the story specifically to give them opportunity to even get the methodical approach you described. That is to even get the path's basic functionality going.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I don't think the methodical approach would be harmed if the ST went the opposite route completely. If an ST replaced quintessence with the old mana rules, booted out turn-per-do completely, and implemented the simplified aspects system in the book(each success equals [path] dots to put in an aspect), the most roided-out sorcerer would still have limited willpower pool, less direct combat strength than most supernaturals if they relied on fast-cast spells as opposed to rituals and artifacts, and a need to avoid drawing attention to themselves to not get overwhelmed by a much larger force. The methodical approach and reliance on mundane tools to conserve resources would still be there in spades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T15:36:05-07:00","id":1495379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495375#post1495375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can understand your point, but I don't think this book accomplishes what you envision.<br /> <br /> Mages are able to do the slow methodical route as well, And do it vastly better than sorcerers. Enchanted objects, rituals and personal empowerments are all things mages do better in addition to fast-casting, which becomes even more of an issue with the fact that the XP costs for both are comparable. If sorcerers were given a way to equal what mages accomplish via the slow, methodical route or were given much more of and XP brake so that they could advance faster and/or branch out more, I'd agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerers are no more equal to mages than ghouls are to vampires. Or perhaps more accurately Kinfolk to werewolves. One on one, they are not designed to be on a level playing field. But that's design intent, if that's not fun at your table, shift it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495375#post1495375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think needing difficult and rare components for even the low levels of a path to work is too much personally, even without other factors. From a play standpoint, a player would either see very little use of the path or would need to invest heavily in it with the ST shaping the story specifically to give them opportunity to even get the methodical approach you described. That is to even get the path's basic functionality going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tass is a toggle you can easily control as the Storyteller. How much Tass is around? Well, that's up to you. You can make Tass common, set up an elaborate economy of sorcerers trading Tass, build early adventures around doing grunt work for a mage in order to score Tass, there are about a thousand story ideas there if you want to explore them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495375#post1495375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, I don't think the methodical approach would be harmed if the ST went the opposite route completely. If an ST replaced quintessence with the old mana rules, booted out turn-per-do completely, and implemented the simplified aspects system in the book(each success equals [path] dots to put in an aspect), the most roided-out sorcerer would still have limited willpower pool, less direct combat strength than most supernaturals if they relied on fast-cast spells as opposed to rituals and artifacts, and a need to avoid drawing attention to themselves to not get overwhelmed by a much larger force. The methodical approach and reliance on mundane tools to conserve resources would still be there in spades.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, what you describe sounds like a Mage. We wanted to ensure a strong mechanical distinction for another style of play. But the system is built to withstand a lot of optional approaches and still work. Changing the Quintessence economy, for example, won't make the wheels fall off. You should be able to tweak the material pretty severely and still have functionality and playability.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T16:58:15-07:00","id":1495386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495379#post1495379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerers are no more equal to mages than ghouls are to vampires. Or perhaps more accurately Kinfolk to werewolves. One on one, they are not designed to be on a level playing field. But that's design intent, if that's not fun at your table, shift it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to ask because you said this before and I don't understand how that coincides what you said later:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495379#post1495379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, what you describe sounds like a Mage. <b>We wanted to ensure a strong mechanical distinction for another style of play</b>. But the system is built to withstand a lot of optional approaches and still work. Changing the Quintessence economy, for example, won't make the wheels fall off. You should be able to tweak the material pretty severely and still have functionality and playability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was the design choice to have sorcerers a ghoul equivalent to mages or to make them their own unique thing?<br /> <br /> I dont really understand how having them be mage-ghouls is compatible with their ability to be unique.<br /> <br /> Making them their own thing, but intentionally making them distinctly inferior to any full splat in addition to that, harms my ability to run them as their own unique thing in a setting where other options exist. This is especially true for me as an avid crossover ST and player who uses sorcerer in place of mage to keep the mechanics coherent(mage is very bad about unbalancing this kind of game unfortunately)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495379#post1495379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tass is a toggle you can easily control as the Storyteller. How much Tass is around? Well, that's up to you. You can make Tass common, set up an elaborate economy of sorcerers trading Tass, build early adventures around doing grunt work for a mage in order to score Tass, there are about a thousand story ideas there if you want to explore them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe there problems with that though. That also puts more of a workload on the storyteller that could be used for keeping track of other things rather than the amount of tass, it's resonance, and how helpful that will be to a player at a specific time. It's another added layer of bookkeeping that could be fun for a story centered around that, but can bog down stories with another focus.<br /> <br /> With mana, It's simple and kept track of by the player.<br /> <br /> I can mod that at my table sure, but what I do at my table isn't standard and I can't guarantee how a game will play when I go to another table. I don't have faith in a book if I have to house-rule it heavily to make it fun to play alongside other books that simply are fun on their own merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T17:54:50-07:00","id":1495393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495386#post1495386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to ask because you said this before and I don't understand how that coincides what you said later:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Was the design choice to have sorcerers a ghoul equivalent to mages or to make them their own unique thing?<br /> <br /> I dont really understand how having them be mage-ghouls is compatible with their ability to be unique.<br /> <br /> Making them their own thing, but intentionally making them distinctly inferior to any full splat in addition to that, harms my ability to run them as their own unique thing in a setting where other options exist. This is especially true for me as an avid crossover ST and player who uses sorcerer in place of mage to keep the mechanics coherent(mage is very bad about unbalancing this kind of game unfortunately)</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see how that could use some clarification. The differential in power/ability between a sorcerer and a Mage are equivalent to those of a Kinfolk and a Garou. Sorcerers are not meant to stand toe to toe, one on one with a Mage. They are mechanically, conceptually, and as a matter of raw potency, distinct. If you are using sorcerer as a stand in for Mages in a crossover that's fine, but that's also not what they're designed for. You'll have to adjust accordingly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495386#post1495386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there problems with that though. That also puts more of a workload on the storyteller that could be used for keeping track of other things rather than the amount of tass, it's resonance, and how helpful that will be to a player at a specific time. It's another added layer of bookkeeping that could be fun for a story centered around that, but can bog down stories with another focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it? Is there a reason the player wouldn't track their Tass? If it's the focus of a story, I would think there would be incentive to keep track of what it was and how it works. Tass and its uses are nothing new to the setting, but this book makes them important in a way that, in my opinion, hasn't really been done mechanically and thematically in the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495386#post1495386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With mana, It's simple and kept track of by the player.<br /> <br /> I can mod that at my table sure, but what I do at my table isn't standard and I can't guarantee how a game will play when I go to another table. I don't have faith in a book if I have to house-rule it heavily to make it fun to play alongside other books that simply are fun on their own merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also can't guarantee what anyone will do at their table. All I can do is convey the concepts as I and the creative team see them best implemented to deliver the experience we are aiming to create. I don't see any issues with Tass and Resonance because they've been attached to magic(k) since there's been magic(k). We are just leveraging it in a new, hopefully exciting way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T03:14:27-07:00","id":1495412,"title":"","content":"Frankly, my single biggest \u201ccomplaint\u201d with the removal of the Mana Background with nothing to replace it is that it doesn't support the playstyle that Sorcerer Revised did. As I see it, M20 products are supposed to be backward compatible; you might change <i>how</i> some things are done from older editions, possibly even relegating some previous choices to \u201coptional rule\u201d status (preferably with some explanation as to why); but you shouldn't change <i>if</i> they're done at all. When I have to go back to SRev to do something that S20 doesn't allow, that's a defect in S20. <br /> <br /> That said, what's done is done. And I have S:PoP, which doesn't try to dictate a particular playstyle to me. I'm just disappointed that S20 <i>does</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T08:03:21-07:00","id":1495430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495412#post1495412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, my single biggest \u201ccomplaint\u201d with the removal of the Mana Background with nothing to replace it is that it doesn't support the playstyle that Sorcerer Revised did. As I see it, M20 products are supposed to be backward compatible; you might change <i>how</i> some things are done from older editions, possibly even relegating some previous choices to \u201coptional rule\u201d status (preferably with some explanation as to why); but you shouldn't change <i>if</i> they're done at all. When I have to go back to SRev to do something that S20 doesn't allow, that's a defect in S20.<br /> <br /> That said, what's done is done. And I have S:PoP, which doesn't try to dictate a particular playstyle to me. I'm just disappointed that S20 <i>does</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's completely fair. We made design decisions that I feel support most styles of play while clarifying the differences between hedge magic and True Magick, and also providing casting rules that allow for personalization of character through Paradigm while keeping all Path Magic running on the same engine. The function and description of the Mana Background didn't fit with the narrative or mechanical vision we set out to create. We included Artifact precisely because it functions on its own set of rules, mechanically distinct from Wonder. Having said that, you can always use the Mana Background from Revised or the Avatar/Genius background from M20 to grant sorcerers a Quintessence pool in your game.<br /> <br /> As for the backwards compatibility argument, I'm not sure I follow your point. You *can* use the Mana Background from Revised if you choose to. If you want to stick completely to M20, use the Avatar/Genius Background from M20. It's not included in the official list because sorcerers don't have Awakened Avatars. The only mechanical element that Background provides is the ability to absorb, store, and spend Quintessence. What this says to me is that those are the mechanical functions of the Awakened Avatar, so it doesn't make much sense to have sorcerers have the same ability under a different name.<br /> <br /> But you don't have to go to a previous edition to make M20 Sorcerer work the way you want it to. You only need to add a single word to a single list on p. 104<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T11:27:06-07:00","id":1495447,"title":"","content":"I've always taken it as a given that, barring Gilgul or an equivalent extraordinary circumstances, every human has an Avatar. For most Sleepers, the ability to store and channel Quintessence isn't something they'd have much use for; they don't have any way of spending it, and nobody has any way of taking it from them. So for most Sleepers, it's not so much that they can't take it as that there's little point in taking it. <br /> <br /> But sorcerers, though Sleepers, are different: with their Hedge Paths, they <i>do</i> have something that they can spend Quintessence on. Likewise, characters with The Flow of Ki, Force of Spirit, or Strength of Psyche have things they can spend Quintessence on, and so the Avatar Background becomes relevant to them. <br /> <br /> What's different between a sorcerer's Avatar and a mage's Avatar isn't whether or not it's capable of storing Quintessence; it's whether the Avatar is dormant or active \u2014 that is, the narrative aspects of having an Awakened Avatar: its tendency to involve itself in your life and to push you to grow. And unless you have Manifest Avatar or something similar, that's not much of a difference: by default, the narrative effect of the Avatar is subtle and easy to miss. <br /> <br /> In short, I <i>do</i> think that it makes sense for sorcerers to be able to access the mechanical benefits of the Avatar Background, but not the narrative effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T11:52:13-07:00","id":1495453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495430#post1495430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's completely fair. We made design decisions that I feel support most styles of play while clarifying the differences between hedge magic and True Magick, and also providing casting rules that allow for personalization of character through Paradigm while keeping all Path Magic running on the same engine. The function and description of the Mana Background didn't fit with the narrative or mechanical vision we set out to create. We included Artifact precisely because it functions on its own set of rules, mechanically distinct from Wonder. Having said that, you can always use the Mana Background from Revised or the Avatar/Genius background from M20 to grant sorcerers a Quintessence pool in your game.<br /> <br /> As for the backwards compatibility argument, I'm not sure I follow your point. You *can* use the Mana Background from Revised if you choose to. If you want to stick completely to M20, use the Avatar/Genius Background from M20. It's not included in the official list because sorcerers don't have Awakened Avatars. The only mechanical element that Background provides is the ability to absorb, store, and spend Quintessence. What this says to me is that those are the mechanical functions of the Awakened Avatar, so it doesn't make much sense to have sorcerers have the same ability under a different name.<br /> <br /> But you don't have to go to a previous edition to make M20 Sorcerer work the way you want it to. You only need to add a single word to a single list on p. 104</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you needed a simple paragraph or two on adjusting the Sorcerers to needs. Many people do like using Sorcerers as replacement Mages. And some people prefer things spelt out. <br /> <br /> Myself, I find it a good job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T12:46:56-07:00","id":1495455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495447#post1495447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always taken it as a given that, barring Gilgul or an equivalent extraordinary circumstances, every human has an Avatar. For most Sleepers, the ability to store and channel Quintessence isn't something they'd have much use for; they don't have any way of spending it, and nobody has any way of taking it from them. So for most Sleepers, it's not so much that they can't take it as that there's little point in taking it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That maybe how you run it at your table, but that's not how M20 presents it. The Avatar/Genius background strictly refers to the Awakened Avatar. You can alter that in your game, but that's just not accurate to the metaphysics of the setting as presented throughout the line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495447#post1495447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, I <i>do</i> think that it makes sense for sorcerers to be able to access the mechanical benefits of the Avatar Background, but not the narrative effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then let your sorcerers take Avatar/Genius","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T12:51:18-07:00","id":1495457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495453#post1495453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps you needed a simple paragraph or two on adjusting the Sorcerers to needs. Many people do like using Sorcerers as replacement Mages. And some people prefer things spelt out.<br /> <br /> Myself, I find it a good job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for saying as much. The ship has sailed on the final text for Sorcerer, but I always appreciate feedback on how I might present things more clearly in the future.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T14:20:09-07:00","id":1495458,"title":"","content":"I think I was more hoping for a &quot;World of Darkness: Sorcerer&quot; that would have meshed better with the Ghost Hunters/Hunters Hunted side of things than a pure supplement for M20. The book is good as a companion to Mage and I'm sure that was the brief, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 10-22-2022, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T14:51:42-07:00","id":1495460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495455#post1495455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That maybe how you run it at your table, but that's not how M20 presents it. The Avatar/Genius background strictly refers to the Awakened Avatar. You can alter that in your game, but that's just not accurate to the metaphysics of the setting as presented throughout the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cThroughout the line\u201d doesn't consider how the Backgrounds apply to Sleepers, one way or the other. In the M20 books, only <b>Gods and Monsters</b> and <b>Sorcerer</b> have had anything to say about non-mages. <br /> <br /> I would submit that having sorcerers interact with Quintessence <i>at all</i> is not accurate to how the metaphysics were presented in earlier editions: that's the reason why SRev spoke of Mana instead of Quintessence. So S20 is arguably <i>already tweaking</i> the metaphysics in terms of how Quintessence and Quintessence-related traits relate to sorcery. Even if I were to agree with your statement that the Avatar Background has previously been used specifically to refer only to Awakened Avatars, it would be a vet minor tweak, and one fully in keeping with the Quintessence related changes you've already made, to make the Avatar Background available to sorcerers as well as mages. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495455#post1495455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then let your sorcerers take Avatar/Genius</div> </div> </div> </div>I already said that I will, in my very first post in this thread. That doesn't change my opinion that you should have added that one word to p.104 in the published text instead of telling the fans to do it themselves \u2014 and not even addressing the issue in the book at all. <br /> <br /> I apologize if I'm coming across a little harshly; that's not my intent. The squeaky wheel gets the grease, so my comments trend to lean towards criticism \u2014 not because I don't think that you've done anything right, but because the things you've done right don't require any action. With that said, I <i>like</i> the fact that you replaced SRev's Mana with Quintessence; it's a change from earlier metaphysics, but a welcome one. <br /> <br /> But I <i>do</i> think you made a mistake in taking out the Mana Background from the earlier edition and not replacing it with anything; and your explanations as to why you did it don't change the fact that we can't use S20 as is to do something that we were able to do in SRev. <br /> <br /> I realize that it's too late to change anything now; but that's part of why I wish you could have gotten feedback a lot earlier in the process than when the advance copies went out. We could potentially have hashed this out back when it mattered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T15:36:17-07:00","id":1495461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495458#post1495458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I was more hoping for a &quot;World of Darkness: Sorcerer&quot; that would have meshed better with the Ghost Hunters/Hunters Hunted side of things than a pure supplement for M20. The book is good as a companion to Mage and I'm sure that was the brief, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand the desire for that framing. We did try to comprehensively collect all groups that use hedge magic or psychics from across the lines, such as the inclusion of Project Twilight. This book should function across the WoD, but is, ultimately, a Mage supplement.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T15:47:50-07:00","id":1495464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495460#post1495460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cThroughout the line\u201d doesn't consider how the Backgrounds apply to Sleepers, one way or the other. In the M20 books, only <b>Gods and Monsters</b> and <b>Sorcerer</b> have had anything to say about non-mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is becoming a bit circular. M20 describes the Awakened Avatar. In sorcerer, we sought to reconcile the metaphysics with the setting as presented both historically and in the new directions we wanted to explore. I feel we have done that. I'm sorry that it wasn't in the way you were looking for. I respect your opinion, and understand where you're coming from, but it's not ultimately the direction we chose to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495460#post1495460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize if I'm coming across a little harshly; that's not my intent. The squeaky wheel gets the grease, so my comments trend to lean towards criticism \u2014 not because I don't think that you've done anything right, but because the things you've done right don't require any action. With that said, I <i>like</i> the fact that you replaced SRev's Mana with Quintessence; it's a change from earlier metaphysics, but a welcome one.<br /> <br /> But I <i>do</i> think you made a mistake in taking out the Mana Background from the earlier edition and not replacing it with anything; and your explanations as to why you did it don't change the fact that we can't use S20 as is to do something that we were able to do in SRev.</div> </div> </div> </div>No apologies necessary, and I apologize if i seem curt, short, or anything but welcoming in my responses. I understand what you're saying, and if I had a time machine, I would go in and expand on why that choice was made, and perhaps some more explicit options for sorcerers to address Quintessence. If I get the chance to address the topic again, I will do that very thing, but ultimately, I stand by the decisions and the reasoning behind them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495460#post1495460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize that it's too late to change anything now; but that's part of why I wish you could have gotten feedback a lot earlier in the process than when the advance copies went out. We could potentially have hashed this out back when it mattered.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Backgrounds section was one of the most heavily discussed sections during the feedback process. Don't feel like this issue didn't get brought up in time. We hashed it out, and there were tweaks made based on that feedback, but the decision with Mana was simple: it mechanically did the same thing as Avatar, which sorcerers should not mechanically have, so we removed it.<br /> <br /> Thank you very much though for all the feedback though. The aim as always is to make as many of the fans as happy as possible!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":25411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","user":"TravisLegge","date":".  typos 10-22-2022, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T21:13:21-07:00","id":1495467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495461#post1495461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand the desire for that framing. We did try to comprehensively collect all groups that use hedge magic or psychics from across the lines, such as the inclusion of Project Twilight. This book should function across the WoD, but is, ultimately, a Mage supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just wish someone had consolidated the &quot;mortal sidekick/adversary&quot; rules back in the day, I think. Sometimes mortals use conscience/self-control/conviction, sometimes they don't! Numina get renamed between books. Merits all over the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T08:32:36-07:00","id":1495479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495467#post1495467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I just wish someone had consolidated the &quot;mortal sidekick/adversary&quot; rules back in the day, I think. Sometimes mortals use conscience/self-control/conviction, sometimes they don't! Numina get renamed between books. Merits all over the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely understand. We tried to collect as much as possible in Sorcerer. While the material is all filtered through a Mage lens, you could always incorporate morality traits if that suits the game you are running. To my mind those traits are directly related to the struggle with the Beast (mechanically and thematically, a non-issue outside the context of Vampire) but if you wanted to emphasize that in play, nothing would be diminished in the Sorcerer rules by incorporating those traits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T17:35:01-07:00","id":1495504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495178-m20-sorcerer-dropped-what-are-everyone-s-thoughts?p=1495479#post1495479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I absolutely understand. We tried to collect as much as possible in Sorcerer. While the material is all filtered through a Mage lens, you could always incorporate morality traits if that suits the game you are running. To my mind those traits are directly related to the struggle with the Beast (mechanically and thematically, a non-issue outside the context of Vampire) but if you wanted to emphasize that in play, nothing would be diminished in the Sorcerer rules by incorporating those traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I think they're basically unnecessary dogwater even for Vampire, I just have an aesthetic need for consolidation and symmetry in my rules, whenever possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-26T10:40:13-07:00","id":1495622,"title":"","content":"So my book arrived and I went through it and despite my initial 'worry' about things the changes I made were actually much less than I feared they would be based on quick glancing and also my changes to the previous edition. Going from start to end these were the sticky notes I made into the book.<br /> <br /> <b>Casting Rules</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Dice Pool: Attribute + Ability<br /> Cost: 1 Willpower<br /> Time: 1 Turn per 2 Path levels.<br /> Difficulty: Path level + 3.</div>I used some of the sidebars from Sorcerer Revised to make the above. I also wrote this out because the info is in a paragraph and not in a sidebar or in an immediately seen section.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspects</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Distance - Less a house rule and more a note, but I am all for allowing scores or hundreds of miles to be teleported through if one wants to say travel regional or continental distances.<br /> Passengers - Move dots upward. So o is &quot;Yourself, your clothing, and a small amount of stuff&quot; and ooooo is &quot;Five passengers&quot;. I have less than zero interest in not allowing clothes to transport with the person.</div>I might do some changes to some of them but in general they work as they are.<br /> <br /> <b>Complications</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Simplified Aspect - Always considered in play. Never a time when it won't.<br /> Witnesses - These do not matter! A sorcerer can cast their magic in the middle of a baseball stadium and disbelief will have ZERO impact.<br /> Fast Casting - Is obviously changed slightly due to the 1 turn per two Path levels rule change.</div>My only other note is that all the modifications, minus Witnesses, are applied.<br /> <br /> <b>Paths</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Conjuration - The modifier section about Witnesses was removed.<br /> Divination - Less a house rule and more an easier way to implement things. So I am thinking of bring over the Trinity idea of 'Dramatic Editing'. This would represent 'I planned ahead'. Maybe successes on a Divination roll would grant a pool of successes that can be used at other points.<br /> Fascination - If dislike/hate can add to the difficulty then like/loved can decrease difficulty. Also I added a note that Duration is an acceptable Aspect.<br /> Healing - I didn't so much change as add this note: Mostly so I can easily see what can be spent and for what.</div><div style=\"margin-left:80px\"><br /> 1 success per Bashing<br /> 1 success per 2 Lethal<br /> 1 success per other healing<br /> +1 for Aggravated<br /> +2 for Regeneration<br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Hellfire - Spells take One turn to cast.<br /> Quintessence Manipulation - Spells cast in/at a Node have reduced Difficulties based on rating.</div>I didn't make any notes on Psychic Paths or the Practitioners chapter.<br /> <br /> I will note that I really like how Psychic Hypnosis works and I also really like the Arcanum group.<br /> <br /> I will also note that if I was to run a Sorcerer game I would not touch the Traditions/Technocracy at all. Maybe there could be an Elder Sorcerer with special abilities but yeah, as it is Awakened Magic would not be a focus or have a presence in such a game.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Creation</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Process - I'm using the variant rules in Revised for point spread. That is 7/5/3 Attributes, 13/9/5 Abilities, 7 Backgrounds, 6 Numina, 15 Freebies.<br /> Secondary Numina - I'm removing this 21 XP cost surcharge. If you want to spread out between sorcery and psychic stuff go right ahead at normal cost.<br /> Backgrounds - Those available to Traditions can be gotten by anyone, no need to restrict Chantry, Node, Retainers, and Sanctum.<br /> Avatar - I am specifically bringing back the Avatar background to represent personal Quintessence collection. I'm thinking of adding a / to the name for all that mechanically its the same.<br /> Merits - I specifically made a note that these are available and that they cost 3 XP per dot.</div>And that's it. Most of my notes are clarifications rather than outright changes.<br /> <br /> So yeah basically I really enjoyed the book and I am glad it was made and that I have it in my collection. Multiple ideas came to me while reading the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 10-26-2022, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T08:57:05-07:00","id":1495829,"title":"","content":"While I am satisfied with M20: Sorcerer, I still plan to use Sorcerer:Paths of Power and Sorcerer's Companion books for my own personal games I run to help house rule things I would have liked to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T07:12:20-07:00","id":1495879,"title":"","content":"I also want to state that I want sorcery to be slow, methodical, and heavily ritualistic. It is why I prefer sorcery to mage because I feel mage is too much like playing a demi-god especially at high level. Sorcery, even at high levels still keeps that occultic and wizard feel to it. But this should not mean that sorcery should be weaker or inferior or not &quot;real magic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-03T19:22:16-07:00","id":1496180,"title":"","content":"Sorcerer worked just fine for me in core WoD games like V:tM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}